Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:04.37,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Now film the trajectory,\None frame every two time units.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:04.45,0:00:06.65,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Neighbouring frames look alike.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.73,0:00:08.50,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Cut the film into frames.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:08.58,0:00:12.99,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Drop them in a shoebox, shake,\Nand throw away the timestamps.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.07,0:00:16.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Pour the box out:\Nthe frames redraw the same glow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.66,0:00:21.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Each frame is a snapshot:\Nthree dial readings, nothing more.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.68,0:00:24.41,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}It carries no timestamp and no time order.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.49,0:00:28.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Yet the shoebox, plus the equations,\Nanswers many questions.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:28.51,0:00:32.89,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Averages, energy budgets, even\Nhow often the dipole crosses zero.
